@startuml overview
' cumin-works - the states of an implementation issue in the review stage.
' A state is a label on GitHub, written without "cumin/status/". "do /" says who works in the state.
' A transition is written: action [guard] / what cumin does. A gray state belongs to another area.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "checking" as Checking #EEEEEE
Checking : (the implementation area)

state "reviewing" as Reviewing
Reviewing : do / the Reviewer reviews the pull request

state "implementing" as Implementing #EEEEEE
Implementing : (the implementation area)

state "awaiting-decision" as Decision
Decision : do / the Assignee answers

state "merging, awaiting-merge-decision,\nor awaiting-blocker-merge" as Merge #EEEEEE
Merge : (the merge area)

Checking --> Reviewing : request the review\n[every required check completed]\n/ cumin starts the Reviewer
Reviewing --> Implementing : request a review fix\n[the review completed with REQUEST_CHANGES,\nbelow the limit]\n/ cumin starts the Implementer\nin the same session
Reviewing --> Checking : go back to the checks\n[the Reviewer run has ended, and: the head commit changed,\nor APPROVE but the required checks have not completed]
Reviewing --> Reviewing : request the review again\n[the Reviewer run has ended, no review on the head commit,\nno question, first time]\n/ cumin starts the Reviewer again
Reviewing --> Decision : stop at the round limit\n[the review completed with REQUEST_CHANGES\nat the limit]\n/ cumin notifies
Reviewing --> Decision : stop the review\n[the Reviewer run has ended, and: the Reviewer asked,\nor no review after the retry,\nor not exactly one risk label, or no pull request]\n/ cumin notifies
Reviewing --> Merge : [the review completed with APPROVE,\nthe required checks completed]

@enduml
